WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.860
In UK law, embryo research
must stop by day 14,

2
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.380
around when a line called
the primitive streak forms.

3
00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:13.220
In August 1945, nuclear weapons
were used on two cities,

4
00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.480
Hiroshima and Nagasaki.

5
00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:18.720
Christians teach that
every human life is sacred,

6
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.820
made in the image of God.

7
00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:23.750
So can a Christian ever support a war?

8
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.280
Or research on an embryo
just five days old?

9
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:30.580
In this mission, you'll trace
how a human life develops,

10
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.330
and how different
Christians judge its worth.

11
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:38.380
Then you'll put weapons of mass destruction
through the tests of just war theory.

12
00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:43.540
Your mission: weigh up how Christians
apply the sanctity of life to embryos and

13
00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:44.360
to war.
